Suppress DT_MIPS_RLD_MAP_REL for IRIX output

The decompiled native MIPSpro linker knows DT_MIPS_RLD_MAP (0x70000016),
DT_MIPS_COMPACT_SIZE (0x7000002f) and DT_MIPS_GP_VALUE (0x70000030) but
has no DT_MIPS_RLD_MAP_REL (0x70000035); the tag was added upstream in
a5499fa4649e4325cf46edfff2f24dae2fe2afef (Matthew Fortune, 2015-06-11,
"Add support for DT_MIPS_RLD_MAP_REL.") for PIE debugging. IRIX 6.5.7's
o32 loader predates it, and 2.47 emits it unconditionally for
executables, so every 2.47 o32 hello's .dynamic carries one extra entry
(21 vs the working 2.20.1 link's 20). Gate the tag on !SGI_COMPAT so IRIX
output keeps only DT_MIPS_RLD_MAP with the 2.20.1 dynamic layout; generic
MIPS/Linux keeps the tag unchanged.

Effect (cand-h): .dynamic back to 20 entries, DT_MIPS_RLD_MAP only;
see docs/binutils.md. Guest validation pending.

--- a/bfd/elfxx-mips.c
+++ b/bfd/elfxx-mips.c
@@ -10285,7 +10285,12 @@
 	  && !MIPS_ELF_ADD_DYNAMIC_ENTRY (info, DT_MIPS_RLD_MAP, 0))
 	return false;
 
+      /* IRIX 6.5's o32 loader predates DT_MIPS_RLD_MAP_REL (added in
+	 2015); emitting it pushes .dynamic past the 2.20.1 layout and
+	 the loader rejects the executable at startup.  Keep the tag for
+	 generic MIPS/Linux and leave SGI output at DT_MIPS_RLD_MAP.  */
       if (bfd_link_executable (info)
+	  && !SGI_COMPAT (info->output_bfd)
 	  && !MIPS_ELF_ADD_DYNAMIC_ENTRY (info, DT_MIPS_RLD_MAP_REL, 0))
 	return false;
 
